    "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
    "note": "The plan's own source (wave-1 row 34). Same zip and Blender route as the elephant and lion, with Textures/colormap.png as an extra member and maxColors 64. Compared with the Quaternius Textured Cute Monster Pack penguin (OpenGameArt, CC0, Blends/Penguin.blend, ingested and rendered side by side): that one is a round head-only blob with no legs or feet and huge eyes, which reads as a monster more than a penguin; the Kenney cube pet stands upright on orange feet with flippers, a white front and a beak, so it reads as a penguin at a glance and ships. Look: the eyes are flat discs in the same dark grey as the body (they cannot be split by colour), so the body uses threshold 0.55 and faceted shading: the eye discs then always fall in the near-black shade and stay black through every clip, instead of flickering to navy when the head tilts up. All greys -> body, whites -> belly, oranges -> beak and feet."
  },
